    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.98,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.5 from 4 h to 18 h, which suggests the reader is saturating. I diluted the retained 18 h aliquot to check. At 10x dilution the reads were 0.189 and 0.198, which scales to about 1.93. At 40x dilution the read was 0.049, which scales to about 1.97. The two dilutions agree with each other, so the diluted readings are in the linear range. The true OD at 18 h is about 1.95, roughly 4x the undiluted reading of 0.506. The flat 0.5 plateau is a detector ceiling, not a stationary culture at that level."
